# ncdu. Read from ~/.config/ncdu/config; one command-line option per line.
# Every option here is in the ncdu(1) man page shared by the 1.x and 2.x
# branches. `--ignore-config` runs without this file.

# Stay on one filesystem: `ncdu /` otherwise walks network mounts, Docker
# volumes and every disk under /Volumes.
-x
# Skip /proc, /sys and cgroup pseudo-filesystems. Linux only; ignored elsewhere.
--exclude-kernfs
# Directories carrying a CACHEDIR.TAG (~/.cache, go, cargo, pip) are listed
# but not counted, which is the honest number.
--exclude-caches
# macOS: do not descend into firmlinks and count the data volume twice.
--exclude-firmlinks

# A stray q after a twenty-minute scan of a full disk should ask first, and
# so should every delete. This is the tool people run as root.
--confirm-quit
--confirm-delete

--color dark-bg
# Percentage and bar, item counts, directories first: what a decision to
# delete needs.
--show-percent
--show-graph
--graph-style eighth-block
--show-itemcount
--group-directories-first
# Read mtime and owner, so m sorts by modification time. About 30% more RAM.
-e

# Not counted, still shown with a < marker.
--exclude .git
--exclude node_modules
--exclude .terraform
--exclude .terragrunt-cache
